{
  "$schema": "../schema.json",
  "spec": "part1-l10",
  "description": "L-10 (A ranking makes many claims, pages/learn/ranking-claims.qmd): expected wrong directions of strict orders that part1.json does not hold. The widget ranks the top n units by posterior mean and evaluates two strict orders of those n units with evaluateReport (the expected wrong count E does not depend on tau): the posterior-mean order and, where the data have estimates, the estimate order; misorderedPairs counts the pairs on which the two orders disagree. Full data sets: the league's estimate order under the teaching posterior (frozen draw, prior SD .15), the KRW race pairs on which the estimate and posterior-mean orders disagree, and the KRW race claims of the posterior-mean order whose error probability is above one half (statedAbove at tau = 1/2, read as a threshold). Subsets for the raw-query read-out cases: the six sites' top four (A to D) through errorArray of their released normal posteriors; the league's top twelve (0-based rows 25, 20, 7, 28, 2, 12, 9, 5, 23, 29, 15, 0 of league-30, in rank order) through errorArray of their teaching posteriors; KRW's top two and top five by race posterior mean (0-based rows 61, 14, 16, 36, 94) through the released race error cells, and KRW's top ten (rows 61, 14, 16, 36, 94, 9, 84, 87, 43, 60) for the answers to What to try, with the pair count of ten units. Settings: the four bounds of the L-10 prediction choices.",
  "license_scope": "author",
  "inputs": {
    "l10.six.top4.E": {"fn":"errorArray","args":[[{"$data":"six-sites","path":"tables.units.mean_A.0"},{"$data":"six-sites","path":"tables.units.mean_A.1"},{"$data":"six-sites","path":"tables.units.mean_A.2"},{"$data":"six-sites","path":"tables.units.mean_A.3"}],[{"$data":"six-sites","path":"tables.units.sd_A.0"},{"$data":"six-sites","path":"tables.units.sd_A.1"},{"$data":"six-sites","path":"tables.units.sd_A.2"},{"$data":"six-sites","path":"tables.units.sd_A.3"}],{"ids":["A","B","C","D"],"criteria":["score_A"]}],"note":"sites A to D (the top four by posterior mean), normal posteriors of score A"},
